WEBVTT

00:00:00.001 --> 00:00:03.419 line:91%
Chapter 5. Run a live test in class.

00:00:04.828 --> 00:00:07.720 line:91%
Press the blue "Start" button at the top.

00:00:08.186 --> 00:00:13.599 line:91%
Choose the lesson. Test 1 is before you teach. Test 2 is after you teach.

00:00:14.062 --> 00:00:16.559 line:91%
Press "Open the waiting room".

00:00:17.018 --> 00:00:28.659 line:91%
The waiting room shows the QR code and the address. Students join. The first time, a new phone waits for your OK: tap the tick. Then the names and animals appear.

00:00:29.117 --> 00:00:35.940 line:91%
While they wait, the phones show today's goal: "I can…". Each student taps a face: can I do this now?

00:00:36.399 --> 00:00:41.739 line:91%
If a student taps the wrong name, press the small cross next to the name to free it.

00:00:42.902 --> 00:00:46.739 line:91%
When everyone is in, press "Start the first question".

00:00:47.194 --> 00:00:54.400 line:91%
The question is on the students' phones, and on the projector if you have one. You see how many students have answered.

00:00:56.653 --> 00:01:03.200 line:91%
Need more time? Press "+15 s". When enough students have answered, press "Close answers".

00:01:03.662 --> 00:01:11.240 line:91%
Press "Reveal answer". You see how the class answered, and the most common wrong answers. This is what you will teach.

00:01:11.695 --> 00:01:16.599 line:91%
Press "Leaderboard" to show the top students, with their points and streaks.

00:01:17.064 --> 00:01:24.280 line:91%
Then press "Next question". After answering, each phone asks: "How sure are you?" Chapter 20 shows it.

00:01:24.744 --> 00:01:29.700 line:91%
Here we jump to the last question. At the end, press "Finish test".

00:01:30.156 --> 00:01:39.200 line:91%
Test 1 has no podium, and no speed points. It is calm: it shows what to teach today. Students try to beat it in Test 2.

00:01:40.402 --> 00:01:45.300 line:91%
Each phone shows the student's score, and says: try to beat it in Test 2!

00:01:45.762 --> 00:01:53.261 line:91%
Press "Done: after class". The results are saved, and one page shows everything to do next, in any order.

00:01:54.428 --> 00:01:59.282 line:91%
The class average, the skills to teach again, and the students who need help.

00:01:59.740 --> 00:02:03.981 line:91%
The students who did not take part, so you can mark them absent.

00:02:04.441 --> 00:02:08.621 line:91%
Bonus points, words to send home, and a worksheet to print.

00:02:09.076 --> 00:02:14.522 line:91%
And the next step: Teach. It opens the lesson plan. Chapter 6 shows it.

00:02:14.981 --> 00:02:21.004 line:91%
Back on Home, the "Start class" box already shows the next step: Teach, then Test 2.
